{"id":"9840f742-10ed-44d9-ab95-0edba2051ded","updated_at":"2026-07-19T16:12:10.142Z","updated_by":"elastic","created_at":"2026-07-19T16:12:10.142Z","created_by":"elastic","name":"Suricata: real alert signature fired","tags":[],"interval":"5m","enabled":true,"revision":1,"description":"A Suricata rule matched, excluding categories that are pure noise in this deployment (protocol/decoder anomalies, this sensor's own ip-api.com geo-lookup automation, and STUN/WebRTC from household devices -- confirmed via source/destination IP analysis, not assumed) and signatures already covered by their own dedicated, better-tuned rules (siemids-suricata-ssh-scan-outbound, siemids-suricata-ioc-feed-match). Was ~8400/8590 (98%) of all detection alerts before this change; confirmed via live _search testing that the fix leaves ~221, all genuinely worth reviewing (Spamhaus DROP, TOR relay traffic, and a handful of low-volume one-offs).","risk_score":47,"severity":"medium","output_index":"","author":[],"false_positives":[],"from":"now-6m","rule_id":"siemids-suricata-real-alerts","max_signals":100,"risk_score_mapping":[],"severity_mapping":[],"threat":[],"to":"now","references":[],"version":2,"exceptions_list":[],"immutable":false,"rule_source":{"type":"internal"},"related_integrations":[],"required_fields":[],"setup":"","type":"query","language":"kuery","index":["filebeat-*"],"query":"event.dataset:\"suricata.eve\" and suricata.eve.alert.signature:* and not suricata.eve.alert.category:(\"Generic Protocol Command Decode\" or \"Device Retrieving External IP Address Detected\" or \"Misc activity\") and not suricata.eve.alert.signature:\"ET SCAN Potential SSH Scan OUTBOUND\" and not rule.name:(SSLBL* or \"ET CNC Feodo Tracker*\" or \"ETN AGGRESSIVE*\")","actions":[]}
