{"id":"75570286-d83a-4dd4-89ce-34c65888b7ad","updated_at":"2026-07-19T16:12:10.219Z","updated_by":"elastic","created_at":"2026-07-19T16:12:10.219Z","created_by":"elastic","name":"Suricata: potential outbound SSH scan","tags":[],"interval":"5m","enabled":true,"revision":1,"description":"ET SCAN Potential SSH Scan OUTBOUND fired, excluding known admin/automation hosts (this workstation, raspberrysrv, skynetpi) and destination traffic to GitHub's SSH range (140.82.112.0/20). Confirmed via live IP analysis: 100% of alerts remaining after the source exclusion alone were git-over-SSH to GitHub (140.82.121.3/.4), from both the admin workstation's wg0-tunnel identity (10.62.7.9, the same physical host captured on a second Suricata interface) and a separate wlan1 household device -- not scanning. Destination-based exclusion covers both without needing to enumerate every tunnel identity of the same device.","risk_score":21,"severity":"low","output_index":"","author":[],"false_positives":[],"from":"now-6m","rule_id":"siemids-suricata-ssh-scan-outbound","max_signals":100,"risk_score_mapping":[],"severity_mapping":[],"threat":[{"framework":"MITRE ATT&CK","tactic":{"id":"TA0007","name":"Discovery","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0007/"},"technique":[{"id":"T1046","name":"Network Service Discovery","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1046/"}]}],"to":"now","references":[],"version":2,"exceptions_list":[],"immutable":false,"rule_source":{"type":"internal"},"related_integrations":[],"required_fields":[],"setup":"","type":"query","language":"kuery","index":["filebeat-*"],"query":"event.dataset:\"suricata.eve\" and suricata.eve.alert.signature:\"ET SCAN Potential SSH Scan OUTBOUND\" and not source.ip:(192.168.100.10 or 192.168.100.2 or 192.168.100.3) and not destination.ip:\"140.82.112.0/20\"","actions":[]}
{"id":"17750aab-137d-4c4d-93cf-c2dccfffac83","updated_at":"2026-07-20T17:43:52.346Z","updated_by":"elastic","created_at":"2026-07-20T08:50:50.129Z","created_by":"elastic","name":"Suricata: threat-intel indicator match (Feodo Tracker / SSLBL / Etnetera)","tags":[],"interval":"5m","enabled":true,"revision":2,"description":"A Suricata alert matched a curated external threat-intel indicator (abuse.ch Feodo Tracker known-active C2 IP, SSLBL known-malicious TLS certificate/JA3 fingerprint, or Etnetera's aggressive IP blacklist) -- not a generic ET/Open heuristic match. Distinct from siemids-suricata-real-alerts: this fires specifically on high-confidence, indicator-based hits.","risk_score":73,"severity":"high","output_index":"","author":[],"false_positives":[],"from":"now-6m","rule_id":"siemids-suricata-ioc-feed-match","max_signals":100,"risk_score_mapping":[],"severity_mapping":[],"threat":[{"framework":"MITRE ATT&CK","tactic":{"id":"TA0011","name":"Command and Control","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0011/"},"technique":[{"id":"T1071","name":"Application Layer Protocol","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1071/","subtechnique":[{"id":"T1071.001","name":"Web Protocols","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1071/001/"}]}]}],"to":"now","references":[],"version":1,"exceptions_list":[],"immutable":false,"rule_source":{"type":"internal"},"related_integrations":[],"required_fields":[],"setup":"","type":"query","language":"kuery","index":["filebeat-*"],"query":"event.dataset:\"suricata.eve\" and event.kind:\"alert\" and (rule.name:SSLBL* or rule.name:\"ET CNC Feodo Tracker*\" or rule.name:\"ETN AGGRESSIVE*\")","actions":[]}
{"id":"948a82b5-d102-4736-a4e3-b1bf9babb56c","updated_at":"2026-07-26T00:00:00.000Z","updated_by":"elastic","created_at":"2026-07-26T00:00:00.000Z","created_by":"elastic","name":"Suricata: known-malicious network traffic (Spamhaus DROP / TOR relay)","tags":[],"interval":"5m","enabled":true,"revision":0,"description":"Traffic matched a Spamhaus DROP-listed (hijacked/malicious) netblock or a known TOR relay/router. Split out of siemids-suricata-real-alerts, where these ~200 hits were previously buried under ~8400 informational/noise alerts (ip-api.com lookups, STUN, protocol-decoder anomalies) and effectively invisible to an analyst. This is currently the single most actionable signal in this deployment's Suricata alert stream.","risk_score":73,"severity":"high","output_index":"","author":[],"false_positives":[],"from":"now-6m","rule_id":"siemids-suricata-known-malicious-netblock","max_signals":100,"risk_score_mapping":[],"severity_mapping":[],"threat":[{"framework":"MITRE ATT&CK","tactic":{"id":"TA0011","name":"Command and Control","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0011/"},"technique":[{"id":"T1090","name":"Proxy","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1090/","subtechnique":[{"id":"T1090.003","name":"Multi-hop Proxy","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1090/003/"}]}]}],"to":"now","references":[],"version":1,"exceptions_list":[],"immutable":false,"rule_source":{"type":"internal"},"related_integrations":[],"required_fields":[],"setup":"","type":"query","language":"kuery","index":["filebeat-*"],"query":"event.dataset:\"suricata.eve\" and suricata.eve.alert.signature:* and (suricata.eve.alert.signature:\"ET DROP*\" or suricata.eve.alert.signature:\"ET TOR*\")","actions":[]}
{"id":"29f8f9d6-f6cf-48fa-8af1-2f0f0996c3d9","updated_at":"2026-07-26T15:30:00.000Z","updated_by":"elastic","created_at":"2026-07-26T15:30:00.000Z","created_by":"elastic","name":"Suricata: URLhaus known-malicious domain queried","tags":[],"interval":"5m","enabled":true,"revision":0,"description":"A DNS query matched abuse.ch URLhaus's known-malicious domain list (https://urlhaus.abuse.ch/downloads/hostfile/), via Suricata's `dataset` feature (sid 9500001, resources/suricata/local-rules/urlhaus-domains.rules) -- not the full URLhaus ruleset, which was tried twice and OOM-killed this deployment (see DEPLOYMENT.md, 2026-07-20). Closes the domain-based IoC gap that was an explicitly open item since then. Verified firing correctly via a live test lookup before this rule was added.","risk_score":73,"severity":"high","output_index":"","author":[],"false_positives":[],"from":"now-6m","rule_id":"siemids-suricata-urlhaus-domain-match","max_signals":100,"risk_score_mapping":[],"severity_mapping":[],"threat":[{"framework":"MITRE ATT&CK","tactic":{"id":"TA0011","name":"Command and Control","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0011/"},"technique":[{"id":"T1071","name":"Application Layer Protocol","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1071/"}]}],"to":"now","references":[],"version":1,"exceptions_list":[],"immutable":false,"rule_source":{"type":"internal"},"related_integrations":[],"required_fields":[],"setup":"","type":"query","language":"kuery","index":["filebeat-*"],"query":"event.dataset:\"suricata.eve\" and suricata.eve.alert.signature:\"IOC URLhaus known-malicious domain queried\"","actions":[]}
{"id":"20530121-3d48-4449-98ca-03207e296812","updated_at":"2026-07-26T15:30:00.000Z","updated_by":"elastic","created_at":"2026-07-26T15:30:00.000Z","created_by":"elastic","name":"Suricata: outbound traffic to Spamhaus DROP-listed netblock","tags":[],"interval":"5m","enabled":true,"revision":0,"description":"Traffic from this network to a Spamhaus DROP-listed (hijacked/malicious) netblock -- e.g. a compromised local device beaconing to C2. `et/open` already covers this same list INBOUND (~80 bundled 'ET DROP Spamhaus DROP Listed Traffic Inbound group N' rules, confirmed via the live compiled ruleset); this rule (sid 9500002, resources/suricata/local-rules/spamhaus-drop-outbound.rules, via Suricata's `iprep` feature -- `dataset` does not support CIDR ranges, confirmed empirically) covers the direction that was uncovered: outbound.","risk_score":73,"severity":"high","output_index":"","author":[],"false_positives":[],"from":"now-6m","rule_id":"siemids-suricata-spamhaus-outbound-match","max_signals":100,"risk_score_mapping":[],"severity_mapping":[],"threat":[{"framework":"MITRE ATT&CK","tactic":{"id":"TA0011","name":"Command and Control","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0011/"},"technique":[{"id":"T1071","name":"Application Layer Protocol","reference":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1071/"}]}],"to":"now","references":[],"version":1,"exceptions_list":[],"immutable":false,"rule_source":{"type":"internal"},"related_integrations":[],"required_fields":[],"setup":"","type":"query","language":"kuery","index":["filebeat-*"],"query":"event.dataset:\"suricata.eve\" and suricata.eve.alert.signature:\"IOC Spamhaus DROP-listed destination (outbound)\"","actions":[]}
